  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We have only one data point (config_001: RNA-only, single profile, PCA → acc 0.485). The most critical unknown is whether the image modality carries complementary signal that can improve classification beyond RNA alone. Without this, we cannot determine whether the large multimodal portion of the search space (configs 016–051) is worth exploring. 2) What this tests: config_016 keeps the RNA pipeline identical to config_001 (PCA n2000, single profile) and adds only the image modality via ResNet-50 with a simple concat fusion. This isolates the effect of adding image information as the sole conceptual change, allowing a direct apples-to-apples comparison against the RNA-only baseline. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: Under a tight budget, the highest-impact question is 'does image help at all?' A positive result validates the multimodal direction and justifies subsequent experiments on image encoder choice, aggregation, and fusion type. A null or negative result would redirect effort toward improving the RNA encoder or profile/aggregation strategy, saving many experiments on multimodal variants that would likely underperform. It is the minimal, single-conceptual-change extension of the baseline, satisfying the principle of isolating one design decision."
}

